jumana el ali and her disabled son have  lived in this camp for internally  displaced people for five years  like many others in syria at the  province they rely on food and medical  aid from abroad  sometimes we receive those eight boxes  and sometimes i sell it to buy bread or  vegetables i'm a widow with a disabled  son he needs medication there's no one  to help me  international aid is transported by road  from neighboring turkey through the  bubble hawa crossing  every week hundreds of eight trucks  crossed this border behind me into  northwest syria to help more than 4  million syrians have been displaced in  their own country  the aid accounts for up to 80 percent of  their food supplies  the need is large only international  bodies like the un can help to contain  famine inside syria  the ukraine war has pushed up wheat and  fuel prices and reduced donations aid  groups say a fair and systematic aid  distribution is impossible without the  un's involvement  we don't want our people to suffer a  humanitarian catastrophe or famine this  possibility would cause a massive exodus  to turkey  moscow has threatened to veto un8  deliveries from turkey since 2014 but  there's no other viable alternative to  the bubble hawa crossing and if it was  to be restricted eight agencies say  millions of lives would be at risk cnm  ka solo al jazeera at the turkish-syrian  border
 

